<section class="section n-why" id="integration-approach">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal" style="text-align:center;max-width:760px;margin:0 auto"><div class="section-label" style="margin:0 auto 14px">Our approach</div><h2>Most integration problems are governance problems</h2><p class="lead" style="margin:0 auto">Two systems holding the same record will eventually disagree. The question is what happens next. Without a defined source of truth, conflicting updates overwrite each other silently and nobody notices until reporting is wrong. We decide which system owns which field before we build anything, then add the logging and alerting that makes failures visible.</p></div>
    <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:28px">
      <div class="card reveal"><div class="card-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-key"></i></div><h4>Defined ownership</h4><p>Every synced field has one system of record. Conflicts resolve by rule, not by whichever update landed last.</p></div>
      <div class="card reveal delay-1"><div class="card-icon orange"><i class="fa-solid fa-bell"></i></div><h4>Visible failures</h4><p>Sync errors trigger alerts rather than sitting in a log nobody opens. You find out when something breaks.</p></div>
      <div class="card reveal delay-2"><div class="card-icon blue"><i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-left"></i></div><h4>Reversible changes</h4><p>Bulk syncs run in a sandbox first and ship with a rollback path. A bad mapping does not become a data recovery project.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section process n-rail" id="integration-process">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="reveal" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><div class="section-label" style="margin:0 auto 14px">How it works</div><h2>From stack audit to live sync</h2></div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step reveal"><div class="step-num">01</div><h4>Audit your stack</h4><p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--grey);margin-top:6px;line-height:1.5">Map every tool, what data moves between them, and where it currently breaks. Identify duplicated data entry and governance gaps.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal delay-1"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--orange)">02</div><h4>Design the data flow</h4><p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--grey);margin-top:6px;line-height:1.5">Define the source of truth for each field, the mapping and transformation logic, and how errors are handled. All of it written down.</p></div>
      <div class="step reveal delay-2"><div class="step-num" style="background:var(--deep-navy)">03</div><h4>Build, test, monitor</h4><p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--grey);margin-top:6px;line-height:1.5">Build in a sandbox, test against real data, deploy with monitoring and alerts, then document it so your team knows what runs where.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:40px;text-align:center" class="reveal"><div style="display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:24px 28px;background:var(--white);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:16px;max-width:640px;width:100%;box-shadow:var(--shadow-sm)"><h3 style="font-size:19px">Need something custom?</h3><p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--grey)">If your system has an API, we can connect it. Private apps, coded workflows, webhooks, and middleware, built with documentation and monitoring included.</p><a href="javascript:void(0)" class="js-open-hs-form btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:6px">Book a free consultation</a></div></div>
  </div>
</section>
